	affiliations = {Semmelweis University Faculty of Health Care, Department of Social Studies on Medicine, and Addictology, 1088 Budapest, vas.u 17, Hungary},
	abstract = {Drug users are set apart from society in many respects. The main field of their status is that drug user thinking is at the same time the cause and consequence of the drug user's way of life. The drug user's behaviour is a representation of an idiosyncratic worldview, which cannot find adequate forms of expression amid the options culturally endorsed by modern society. Drug consumer behaviour, despite its hidden and secretive (albeit increasingly more open) nature, materializes in a societal space and in a network of social relations. At the same time, it may be asked how, to what extent and in what forms drug users interact with society. We have examined two areas of drug-user thinking: temporal dimensions of their world of living, and their drug consumption characteristics in the social space. The conclusion is that the structure and pattern of drug-user thinking according to its temporal and spatial dimensions is basically different from the normal population's way of thinking, which makes work focused on prevention and rehabilitation difficult and challenging. ©Borgis.},
